R"VG(
# deephalls2.vg (D-05): genre.deephalls, continued (its first part in deephalls.vg: a file holds at most 16 KB)
@apart

dh.pn.head (formula people=4)
  NOTICE. The rules of {hall.below}, to be obeyed by all residents:
  Regulations for the lower levels at {$home}, by order of {ruler.the}:
  To all below: the rules, which will be enforced.
  The rules of the shelter, posted on every level:
  (age>=modern) Shelter regulations, {hall.below}, revised:
  (age>=modern darkyears>=1) Standing orders for the deep levels, {$home}, the {#darkyears:ord} year below:
  (age>=modern dark=2) Standing orders for the deep levels, {$home}, for the move below:
dh.pn.item (share=0.65)
  (once) Rations of {dark.food} are given out at the {dh.pn.hour} bell, [on presentation of the ration card|one share to each person|to the head of each household].
  (once) The warm-rock shifts change at the {dh.pn.hour} bell. A worker late to the rock [loses a ration|works the next shift too|is reported to the warden].
  (once) No {fuel} is to be burned in the sleeping levels. The air there is [pumped and counted|short as it is|for breathing].
  (once) Surface doors are opened only for the {dh.party} and only by the [duty keeper|warden of the stair|level warden].
  (once) The lights go down at the evening bell. The children's levels are dark [an hour earlier|at the second bell|after the story].
  (once) Deaths are to be reported to the level warden. The dead are carried up [with the next {dh.party}|on the rest day|by their own families].
  (once) Births are to be reported the same day; a newborn and its mother go to the warm level [for a month|until the child can be carried|at once].
  (once) Water is drawn from the melt tanks [by the {vessel.one.n}, at the call|by each household in turn|twice a day, not more].
  (once) Hoarding [{food}|{fuel}|blankets] is theft from the shelter and is punished as theft.
  (once) The children's hours at the warm rock are from the {dh.pn.hour} bell to the meal; [lessons are held there|nobody else is to use the room then|parents may sit with them].
  (once) The upper rooms are closed. Nobody is to sleep above the [third|second|fourth] level.
  (once) The air shafts are not to be blocked, [whatever the cold|by order of the wardens|even in the worst of the frost].
  (once inv.electric=1) The electric light is for the working levels only[. Lamps elsewhere|; the sleeping levels keep the dark|, and is not to be used for heat].
  (once inv.radio=1) The radio gives the news at [noon|the second bell|the evening meal] on every level.
  (once) Visits to the surface to see the stars are permitted on the rest day, in parties of [four|six|no fewer than three].
  (once) The {dark.food} beds are tended by every household in turn; the turn is posted at {dh.stair}.
  (once) Each person may have one {garment.n} from the stores [twice a year|on request|after the children have had theirs].
  (once) The old library in the {dh.room} is open [after the evening meal|on the rest day]; take nothing out.
  (once) Quarrels over places at the warm rock are brought to the warden and to nobody else.
  (once) The {herd} left are kept on the [lowest|warm] level and are not to be slaughtered without the warden's word.
  (once) Anyone feeling the [cough|fever|cold sickness] goes to the infirmary at once and does not sleep with the household.
  (once) No {pastime} on the sleeping levels; in the {dh.room}, until the second bell.
  (once) Nobody is to go up {dh.stair} past the frost line without a lamp and a rope.
  (once) The {craft} rooms are open to every household for one shift in [five|seven|ten].
  (once) The {drink} ration is for the rest day only, [one {vessel.one.n} each|and not for the children|as before].
dh.pn.hour (people=2)
  first
  second
  third
  morning
  evening
dh.pn.end (formula people=3)
  Keep these rules. The shelter keeps you.
  By order. The wardens will see these rules kept.
  These rules hold until the sun comes back.
  Posted on every level. Do not remove.

# =====================================================================================================================
# the halls' radio, or the announcements read out at the shaft (a cylinder's, a disc's, a reel's)
# =====================================================================================================================

dh.bc.open (formula people=4)
  (inv.radio=1) This is the halls' radio at {$home}, with the announcements for the levels.
  (inv.radio=1) Good morning, below. The announcements for today.
  (inv.radio=1) {$home} calling every level. The news from the warm rock.
  The announcements, read at the head of the shaft, for those who could not come.
  (inv.radio=1) This is {$seat}, calling the halls. Listen for your level.
  (inv.radio=1 darkyears>=1) The evening announcements, {hall.below}, the {#darkyears:ord} year of the dark.
  (inv.radio=1 dark=2) The evening announcements, {hall.below}, as the sun goes.
dh.bc.item (share=0.65)
  (once) Rations today as yesterday: {dark.food}, water by the {vessel.one.n}, the evening meal at the bell.
  (once) The warm rock on the [fourth|third|fifth] level is cooler; the shift there [is to move down to the sixth|will be shortened|goes to the lower face].
  (once) The {dh.party} is back. [All {n} returned|One was hurt on the way down and is in the infirmary|They report the frost thicker at the doors]. The surface stands at the cold it always does.
  (once) The lights on the [lower|upper|east] levels will go down for an hour this evening while the {dh.bc.fix} is mended.
  (once) The air on the [north|west|old] side is bad. Move the sleepers from there to the {dh.room}.
  (once) A child was born last night on the warm level. [Mother and child are well|The child is small but strong|It is the {#n:ord} this month].
  (once) We record the deaths of {n} of us this [week|month]. They go up with the next {dh.party}.
  (once) Children's hours at the warm rock are as usual. [Parents, please keep them to the marked rooms|The story tonight is the one about the sun|Bring the slates].
  (once) The beds of {dark.food} on the [second|lower|warm] level came in [well|thin]. The rations stand.
  (once) The sky party reports {sunway.thing} no longer seen. {sun} is where it was.
  (once) The {festival} gathering will be held in the {dh.room}, the songs low.
  (once) Remember: no {fuel} in the sleeping levels. The air is counted.
  (once inv.radio=1) We are still calling the other halls on the long band. [No answer yet|Static, and once a voice we could not make out|Nothing].
  (once) Lost on the [third|fourth] level: a child's [boot|blanket|{garment.n}]. Bring it to the stores.
  (once) The frost line in {dh.stair} has come down another {n} steps. [Keep the doors shut behind you|The inner door will be moved down|Nobody is to sit on the steps].
  (once) The melt tanks are low. Water by the {vessel.one.n} until the {dh.party} is back.
  (once) The old ones' room by the warm rock is full. [Please make room|The wardens will move the beds|Bring your own blankets].
  (once) The {herd} on the lowest level have [had young|been counted: {n}|been moved nearer the rock].
  (once) Music in the {dh.room} tonight: {instrument}, and [the old songs|the songs of the summers|anyone who can play].
  (once) The infirmary asks that anyone with the cough stay with their household and not come to the meal.
  (once) The {craft} rooms need hands; ask at {dh.stair}.
  (once) Tomorrow is the day the sun last rose, by the count. There will be [a silence at the noon bell|a lamp lit in the {dh.room} at noon|the old songs after the meal].
  (once) {pastime} in the {dh.room} after the meal; the wardens ask that it end by the second bell.
  (once) A {vessel.one.n} of {drink} for every household on the rest day, for {feast.custom}.
dh.bc.fix (people=2)
  pump
  line
  lamp
  (age>=modern) generator
dh.bc.close (formula people=3)
  That is all for today. Keep warm, and keep the rules.
  (inv.radio=1) This has been the halls' radio. Until tomorrow, below.
  The next announcements at the same bell.
  Keep to your levels. Keep warm.

# =====================================================================================================================
# the charter of the deep levels, and its amendments (a drive's, a crystal's)
# =====================================================================================================================

dh.ch.head (formula people=4)
  The charter of {hall.below} at {$home}, agreed by all who live below.
  (age>=futuristic) We who live in the warm levels of {$home} set down how we will live, for as long as the dark lasts.
  (darkyears>=1) The compact of the deep levels at {$home}, in the {#darkyears:ord} year of the dark.
  (dark=2) The compact of the deep levels at {$home}, agreed as the sun went.
  How we live below {$home}: agreed, to be read every year at {festival}.
dh.ch.pre (share=0.8)
  We came down when the sun went, and we will not go up again until it comes back or we are gone.
  We are fewer than we were, and we would rather agree in the dark than be ruled in it.
  The warm rock gives us what heat there is; what follows is how we share it.
  We lost the sun and kept each other; this is how.
  What was above is above. What follows is how we live below it.
  The ones who came down first wrote this; the ones born below have kept it.
  As the old saying went, {proverb}; we have needed it below.
dh.ch.art (share=0.7)
  (2 once) The heat of the deep rock belongs to [everyone below|all of us|every level alike], and to no one more than another.
  (2 once) Every person has a place by {warm.ground}, and no one may [take it away|sell it|be moved from it against their will].
  (once) The {dark.food} of the [vats|beds|lower gardens] are grown by all and eaten by all.
  (once) The air is counted and shared; no one may [close a shaft|keep air for themselves|change the pumps alone].
  (once) Every child born below is taught what [the sun was|a day was|a summer was], and what we lost.
  (once) The dead are taken up to the surface, where the cold keeps them, and their names are kept below.
  (once) The lights burn in the working halls; the sleeping halls keep the dark, as the night was kept above.
  (once) Anyone may go up to see the stars, but no one goes [alone|without a lamp|without telling {dh.stair}].
  (once age>=futuristic) The mind of the levels keeps the count of the days and the air; it may not keep anything else from us.
  (once) {festival} is kept by all, below, without the sun it was for.
  (once) [No one is to be blamed for the sun|Nobody is to be blamed for what the sky did|The going of the sun is no one's fault, and no one is to be made to carry it].
  (once) The water of the melt is common; [no household may store more than it drinks|it is carried in the common {vessel} and in no other|whoever wastes it carries ice for the rest].
  (once) Every level chooses its warden, and may unchoose them at the next reading.
  (once) Work at the rock is shared by all who can; those who cannot are kept by those who can.
  (once) Music, stories and the old songs are kept, as the heat is kept, for everyone, with {instrument} at every gathering.
  (once) The record of the days is kept and read aloud [so that no one forgets how long it has been|at every gathering|on the day the sun last rose].
  (once) No one may be sent up into the cold as a punishment.
  (once) The {craft} of the {people} is taught to every child below, as it was taught above.
  (once) {feast.custom} is kept below, every year, whatever the stores.
dh.ch.end (formula people=3)
  This is the charter. It holds until the sun comes back.
  Agreed below, by all. Read it to the children.
  We keep this together, or we do not keep anything.

dh.am.head (formula people=3)
  (darkyears>=1) Amendment to the compact of {hall.below}, agreed at the {#darkyears:ord} reading:
  (dark=2) Amendment to the compact of {hall.below}, agreed before the last sunrise:
  To the charter of the deep levels at {$home}, these changes, agreed below:
  Changes to the compact, voted on every level and carried:
dh.am.item (share=0.8)
  (once) The rations of {dark.food} are cut by a [quarter|tenth|fifth] until the new beds come in.
  (once) The upper levels are given up; their doors are sealed and the frost let in.
  (once) Children may go up to see the stars from their [tenth|twelfth] year, with a warden.
  (once) The {herd} are to be [killed and their meat shared|kept no longer; the beds need the warmth].
  (once) The {#n:ord} level is closed; its households move down to the warm levels.
  (once) The names of the dead are to be read at {festival}, not only at the burial.
  (once) A second shaft is to be cut to the warm rock below the lowest level.
  (once) The wardens are to be chosen by lot from now on, the votes having become quarrels.
  (once age>=futuristic) The mind of the levels may reduce the lights without a vote when the heat falls.
  (once) Anyone who has not been up to see the stars by their twentieth year is to be taken up once, at least.
  (once) The {drink} stores are to be opened only for {festival} and for the sick.
  (once) Nobody is to wager {food} on {pastime} any more.
dh.am.end (formula people=2)
  Carried below. The charter stands as amended.
  So agreed. Read at the next gathering.
)VG"
